From 270cbb505f6559208f4296522182124e49ecace5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:41:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] usb: xhci: reset_ep: fix misaligned pointer in Set TR
 Dequeue Pointer

reset_ep() computed the Set TR Dequeue Pointer command's address by
ORing the ring's cycle bit into ring->enqueue before passing it to
xhci_trb_virt_to_dma(). That function does pointer arithmetic
(trb - seg->trbs) that requires a properly aligned TRB pointer.
Tainting the low bit first breaks that arithmetic whenever
cycle_state==1, which happens naturally as the ring wraps, producing
a garbage segment offset and tripping the BUG_ON in
xhci_trb_virt_to_dma().

Observed on hardware: this panicked intermittently during interrupt
endpoint polling, correlating with the ring having wrapped at least
once.

abort_td() in this same file computes the same kind of address
correctly: get the DMA address from the clean pointer first, then OR
the cycle bit into the resulting integer. Make reset_ep() do the same.

Signed-off-by: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-ring.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-ring.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-ring.c
index f12790308c..855ae1f308 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-ring.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-ring.c
@@ -531,8 +531,16 @@ static void reset_ep(struct usb_device *udev, int ep_index, unsigned int timeout
 	BUG_ON(TRB_TO_SLOT_ID(field) != udev->slot_id);
 	xhci_acknowledge_event(ctrl);
 
-	addr = xhci_trb_virt_to_dma(ring->enq_seg,
-		(void *)((uintptr_t)ring->enqueue | ring->cycle_state));
+	/*
+	 * OR the cycle bit into the DMA address after computing it, not into
+	 * the pointer beforehand: xhci_trb_virt_to_dma() does pointer
+	 * arithmetic (trb - seg->trbs) that requires proper TRB alignment,
+	 * and tainting the low bit first breaks that whenever cycle_state==1
+	 * (which happens naturally as the ring wraps). abort_td() below
+	 * already does this the correct way.
+	 */
+	addr = xhci_trb_virt_to_dma(ring->enq_seg, ring->enqueue);
+	addr |= ring->cycle_state;
 	xhci_queue_command(ctrl, addr, udev->slot_id, ep_index, TRB_SET_DEQ);
 	event = xhci_wait_for_event(ctrl, TRB_COMPLETION, XHCI_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT);
 	if (!event)
